                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.23994/2611.23994v1/method_v4.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Overview of WaveView.The depth warp𝐱\\mathbf{x}of the source (green) and Gaussian noiseϵ\\boldsymbol{\\epsilon}(blue) are decomposed with the DT-ℂ\\mathbb{C}WPT.\nAt a visible location𝐪\\mathbf{q}, the positional uncertainty𝚺⁡(𝐪)\\mathbf{\\Sigma}(\\mathbf{q})is stretched along the epipolar line, so bands whose frequency lies along this line take their phase from the noise, and bands keeping the warp’s phase (green dots) form an ellipse elongated across it.\nThe magnitude of every complex band comes from the noise; holes (𝐯=0\\mathbf{v}=0) are pure noise.\nLower right ofϵ^\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\epsilon}}: the part whose phase comes from the warp.",
                "position": 430
            }
        ]
